# Side-street mouth at the Strobl junction (decorative, NON-solid, engine
# kind Empty, like tunnel_bg; D-038): a dark gap between two house corners
# (i/m and m/d quoins) looking down the road to St. Wolfgang. The street's
# side walls recede to a vanishing point (the shaded one d, the lit one m
# with tiny d windows, eave lines m/n), a strip of sky s/h above them, tiny
# far houses c with n roofs at the end, and the road m with d gutters
# narrowing upwards with w centre dashes. No lip, no light top edge,
# darker and flatter than every solid tile; the cars drive out in front.
# Drawn for a 2-wide, 3-high mouth: the left column (right neighbour only)
# and right column (left only) are the two halves, a column with both
# neighbours shows the middle of the view, a lone column a 16 px version.
# Vertical autotile: the cell with no mouth above shows the rooftops and
# sky, a cell with mouth above and below the walls, the bottom cell the
# road. Generated by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grids
# are the source.
# Autotiled (D-020): anim `auto`, frame = neighbour mask
# (1 = same tile above, 2 = right, 4 = below, 8 = left; level edge = same).
sprite = tile_einfahrt_bg
size   = 16x16
origin = 0,0
anim   = auto frames=16 ticks=1
---
frame auto 0
